{"ts":"2026-09-09T05:47:29+03:00","event":"note","text":"The kind=rubric edit of 3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q16 will stay flagged by 'check --final', deliberately, on the same grounds as the q08/q10/q04 note above. full_sample.3 found that the tail I had added to R0 on 2026-09-08 - 'read from the screen, not reconstructed from an assumed input' - is not checkable, because the judge sees only the answer string and a read answer and a reconstructed one are character-identical. It is replaced by a form requirement, and the sample joins the deferred round rather than being re-run again inside this one. Two further items go with it, from the same review: 'in the substituted row' would be a cleaner discriminator than 'after the shown input substitution' (5.3), and blind_solved must be re-measured, because with R0 now a form requirement it is the only thing standing between a blind model and the answer.","refers_to":"3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q16"}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T05:47:29+03:00","event":"note","text":"Contradiction recorded rather than resolved, found by the adversarial audit and carried into q10's deferred cycle. Three fields of this sample cannot all be right at once. (a) The L1 justification says in so many words that the numeric coefficients are absent from 736 on and that L1 holds by a single-frame read at 728-735 - but 728-735 lies inside the OPTIONAL window [709.0, 735.4], while the REQUIRED window is [736.7, 772.5], where full_window1.10 confirmed on frames that not a single digit is on screen and the x^4 slot sits inside an ellipsis. By 7.3 the level is that of the cheapest route INCLUDING waiting for the required showing, and at the required showing the route is recall, not reading. That is checklist 4.7 - a window that does not answer its own rubric - the very defect this round caught on q03 and did not apply here. (b) Both triggers carry evidence_span [455.0, 470.0], which says the last evidence is at 470; that is coherent with the values being established there and re-displayed later as corroboration, but it is NOT coherent with 'L1 holds by a read at 728-735'. (c) The derived axis 'post' follows from that span, so if the span is stale the axis is wrong too. Which of the three moves is a measurement question, not a desk one: it needs a fresh full_sample on the reworded question that states, for each rubric item, the earliest moment it is available INSIDE the required window. Until then the level, the span and the axis of q10 are all provisional.","refers_to":"3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q10"}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T05:49:37+03:00","event":"finish","agent":"fw1_r14_q03_p2","status":"completed","summary":"FIX_INTERVALS on 7.5, and it REFUTES the first opinion rather than confirming it. Both of the brief's factual questions came back yes - on the cropped frames 226 and 227 all three c1 are sharp, 228 still shows c1 in P(x) and the first derivative line with only the third morphing, 229 has the derivative lines substituted while the P(x) glyph is still in morph, 230 is clean everywhere (a fourth index error on this video: screen_text dates the substitution at 228.0, a ~2 s miss); and 'zero' does run 227.840-228.319, with the antecedent of 'it' ambiguous but harmless. The third question is where it turns: 228.3 is CORROBORATION, not evidence, and the refutation is a frame, not an argument - t000217 carries d(cos)/dx(0) = -sin(0) = 0 and dP/dx(0) = c1 + 2c2*0 side by side, with the tangent-matching goal spoken at 187.4-190.0 and the 'Free to change' callout already gone, so substituting one displayed equality into the other yields c1 = 0 ten seconds before the author says it. Proposed [141.0, 217.0], with 205.0 explicitly acceptable and preferable for consistency. 2.4, 2.5, 3.3 ok, 7.4 na","artifact":"data/reviews/3d6DsjIBzJ4/3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q03/full_window1.14.json"}
