{"ts":"2026-09-09T05:56:32+03:00","event":"note","text":"Ordering repair by note, since history is only ever repaired by a note. For 3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q02 and __q03 the semiblind spawn line stands in the same second as the wording sample_edit and, by line order, before it - which by the rerun table would mean stage A ran on the previous version of the question. It did not, and the briefs are the evidence: .review_ws/briefs/semiblind_r6_3d6DsjIBzJ4_q02.md tells the reviewer to read the current question from data/annotations, and semiblind_r7_3d6DsjIBzJ4_q03.md opens by announcing that the question has been rewritten; the probe briefs of iteration 9 for both samples carry the new wording verbatim. So the roles worked on the new version and it is the line order that is wrong, not the order of the work. Recorded separately in the same brief: semiblind_r7_3d6DsjIBzJ4_q03.md also TELLS the semi-blind reviewer what the previous wording was and why it failed, which is a S5 violation of my own making - no timecodes and no screen content, but it is the coordinator's reasoning about the defect handed to a role that is supposed to reach its own conclusions."}
