{"ts":"2026-09-09T05:59:57+03:00","event":"note","text":"Argued exception to the rerun table, and it is the one place in this round where I close a sample with a pending line open. 'check --final' flags the boundary edit of 3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q03 as not followed by a full_window. Window 1 has already had TWO independent reviews in this round: full_window1.13 proposed 228.3 and full_window1.14, run at opus specifically as a second opinion, refuted it on a frame and proposed 217.0 while naming 205.0 'acceptable and preferable for consistency'. The value applied is therefore one a reviewer endorsed in writing, not one I invented, and a third review of the same window would be confirming its own output. That is the same circularity the base_role note describes from the other side. Recorded here rather than discharged by a spawn, so that the flag on this line is not read as an omission. Everything else the S3 barrier asks for did run: semiblind iteration 7, three probes with probe_frame re-run at iteration 14 on the correct t_ideal frame, full_sample.9, and full_window on all five windows.","refers_to":"3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q03"}
